  </div>

  <div class="narrative">
    <p><span class="highlight">Journal Articles</span> are the dominant publication type, comprising the vast majority of indexed output. Reviews and Systematic Reviews represent a smaller but important segment of the literature, serving as evidence-synthesis resources. Case Reports and Clinical Trials reflect clinical research activity.</p>
    <p>The median of <span class="highlight">""" + f"{median_authors:.0f}" + """ authors per publication</span> signals substantial collaboration in biomedical research. Author counts vary by country, with some nations showing systematically larger research teams. This metric serves as a proxy for collaboration intensity and research network integration.</p>
